{"id": "3.3-00475", "case_id": "t3.5.s1p.1c97937a751dd4e2c340.rhs_844395c82d7d0f28", "parent_id": "t1.3.s1p.1c97937a751dd4e2c340", "source": null, "record_protocol": null, "panels": {"stored": "<h2>Round-trip: Stage 1 → generated text → Stage 2</h2><div class=\"stage-grid\"><div class='card'><div class='stage-step'>STAGE 1</div><h3>Write the whole-module specification</h3><table><tbody><tr><th>Input</th><td>Clean module RTL: <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00475&amp;file=stage1%2Fdesign.v'>stage1/design.v</a></td></tr><tr><th>Instruction</th><td>Describe the interface, parameters, and observable behavior of this clean design. Return a self-contained specification, not RTL implementation code. A separate isolated call will receive your specification.<p class='muted small'>Stored wording: <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00475&amp;file=stage1%2FTASK.md'>stage1/TASK.md</a></p></td></tr><tr><th>Output</th><td><strong>Generated whole-module specification (prose).</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><details><summary>Read input: stage1/design.v · <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00475&amp;file=stage1%2Fdesign.v'>Open raw</a></summary><pre>module  PGAOPV_AN2D2PO4 (\n\t A1\n\t,A2\n\t,Z\n\t);\n\n\t//---------------------------------------\n\t//IO DECLARATIONS\n\ninput\t A1 ;\ninput\t A2 ;\noutput\t Z ;\n\nassign Z = A1 &amp; A2;\n\nendmodule</pre></details></div><div class='card'><div class='stage-step'>STAGE 2</div><h3>Repair the module</h3><table><tbody><tr><th>Input</th><td>The generated Stage 1 text plus buggy mutant rtl: <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00475&amp;file=stage2_template%2Fdesign.v'>stage2_template/design.v</a>. Required top module: PGAOPV_AN2D2PO4.</td></tr><tr><th>Instruction</th><td>Repair the functional fault in design.v using the specification and retained RTL context. Return the complete corrected RTL with the same top module. Only the default configuration is scored.<p class='muted small'>Stored wording: <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00475&amp;file=stage2_template%2FTASK.md'>stage2_template/TASK.md</a></p></td></tr><tr><th>Output</th><td><strong>Complete repaired RTL module.</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><details><summary>Read input: stage2_template/design.v · <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00475&amp;file=stage2_template%2Fdesign.v'>Open raw</a></summary><pre>module  PGAOPV_AN2D2PO4 (\n\t A1\n\t,A2\n\t,Z\n\t);\n\n\t//---------------------------------------\n\t//IO DECLARATIONS\n\ninput\t A1 ;\ninput\t A2 ;\noutput\t Z ;\n\nassign Z = ~(A1 &amp; A2);\n\nendmodule</pre></details></div></div><div class=\"flow\"><strong>Stage 1 output → abstraction gate → fresh Stage 2 input.</strong> The intermediate text is generated separately for each model/attempt. It is not a prefilled golden description. Stage 2 receives neither the clean RTL nor the Stage 1 conversation.</div><h2>Private final evaluation</h2><div class=\"card\"><table><tbody><tr><th style=\"width:175px\">Reference RTL</th><td><a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00475&amp;file=private%2Fgolden.v'>private/golden.v</a></td></tr><tr><th style=\"width:175px\">Score / oracle</th><td>Binary formal equivalence to the hidden clean module</td></tr></tbody></table><p class=\"muted\">The formal oracle consumes the complete Stage 2 RTL file and compares it with the clean reference. A golden RTL file is scoring material, not a generated Stage 1 output.</p></div>"}, "files": [{"name": "case.json", "url": "assets/a1d24d7a0c55f5fa15bac4470c50e5a748521d8c450fe3e9f00225d765e9010e.txt", "size": 4504, "binary": false, "section": "Other: case.json"}, {"name": "private/equivalence.ys", "url": "assets/88573892260d55511de2fee51f9a377865388f23851ea3c59a6aeeea1fddf63d.txt", "size": 623, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/golden.v", "url": "assets/1c97937a751dd4e2c340ae8839b5451230d2dfd235fe944da04dbb3cfe872b10.txt", "size": 175, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/qualification/negative/equivalence.y